# Japanese wording / vocabulary

When writing Japanese documentation, plans, or chat replies for this project:

- Do **not** use「行程」to mean joystick throw, stick travel, or axis range.
- Prefer「フルスケール」「軸レンジ」「可動範囲」「片側フルスケール」など instead.
- Do **not** use「ポール」for GPIO or sensor reads; use the English word `polling`.
- Do **not** use「先端」for a git commit tip; use the English word `head`.

When describing actions that start or stop sound (noteOn/noteOff, 発音, playback/pause, hold-to-sound), in English docs/comments and in Japanese chat or plans:

- Prefer the English word **`trigger`** (e.g. “Blue triggers noteOn/noteOff”, 「Blue で trigger」).
- Do **not** use **`gate`** /「ゲート」for that control sense.
- Keep `gate` only where it is an established DSP/parameter name (e.g. Freezer’s gate input as a product term), not for generic “press to sound / play” wording.
